  "terms": {
    "en": "The verb to be",
    "es": "El verbo ser",
    "it": "Il verbo essere",
    "fr": "Le verbe être",
    "de": "Das Verb sein",
    "ru": "Глагол «быть»",
    "hu": "A „lenni” ige",
    "pt": "O verbo ser",
    "ro": "Verbul „a fi”"
  },
  "locales": {
    "en": {
      "title": "The verb to be",
      "summary": "Be links a subject to a description, a place or an identity.",
      "status": "draft",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "What it is",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "Be is the most important verb in English. It links a subject to a description, a place, an identity or a state."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "I **am** a student.",
                "She **is** tired.",
                "They **are** at home."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "How it works in English",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "Be is irregular: am, is and are in the present; was and were in the past. The short forms are I'm, you're, he's, we're and they're. The negative adds not: isn't, aren't."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "html": "<table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Present</th><th>Past</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>I</strong></td><td><strong>am</strong></td><td><strong>was</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>he, she, it</strong></td><td><strong>is</strong></td><td><strong>was</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>you, we, they</strong></td><td><strong>are</strong></td><td><strong>were</strong></td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "ro": {
      "title": "Verbul „a fi”",
      "summary": "Verbul „a fi” arată existența, starea, identitatea sau locul și are forme diferite pentru fiecare persoană.",
      "status": "draft",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Ce este",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "Verbul „a fi” este cel mai important verb în limba română. El arată identitatea, starea sau locul. Acest verb leagă subiectul de o descriere."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Sunt** student.",
                "Ea **este** obosită.",
                "Copiii **sunt** acasă."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Cum funcționează în română",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "La timpul prezent, verbul „a fi” are forme neregulate. Pronumele precum „eu” sau „tu” nu sunt obligatorii. Pentru o propoziție negativă, punem „nu” înaintea verbului."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "html": "<table><thead><tr><th>Pronume</th><th>Afirmativ</th><th>Negativ</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>(Eu)</strong></td><td><strong>sunt</strong></td><td><strong>nu sunt</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>(Tu)</strong></td><td><strong>ești</strong></td><td><strong>nu ești</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>(El / Ea)</strong></td><td><strong>este / e</strong></td><td><strong>nu este / nu e</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>(Noi)</strong></td><td><strong>suntem</strong></td><td><strong>nu suntem</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>(Voi)</strong></td><td><strong>sunteți</strong></td><td><strong>nu sunteți</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>(Ei / Ele)</strong></td><td><strong>sunt</strong></td><td><strong>nu sunt</strong></td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
